# KNOWN GAP — `Box[Optional[T]]` fails to BUILD on BOTH lanes.
#
#     Box[Optional[String]] b = Box(s.v)
#
#     C    lane: build rc 1, `error: parameter 1 ('val') has incomplete type`
#     LLVM lane: build rc 1
#
# Core #8: both lanes agree the program is unbuildable, and both are wrong --
# `Optional[T]` is an ordinary type and boxing it is ordinary code. Agreement
# on a wrong answer is the trap, not a pass.
#
# Sibling of `box_enum_payload_c_wont_compile_llvm_double_frees.gg` on the
# SAME axis (Box payload type), with a different signature: that one is a C/LLVM
# DIVERGENCE (C won't compile, LLVM compiles and double-frees); this one fails
# UNIFORMLY at build on both. Both were surfaced by enumerating the payload-type
# axis rather than sampling one value of it (Core #12).
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints 1, on BOTH backends.
# Measured 2026-08-27 at HEAD; orchestrator-verified on both lanes.

struct S:
    Optional[String] v

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    S s = S(Some(mk("aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "bbbbbbbb")))
    Box[Optional[String]] b = Box(s.v)
    print(1)
